{"schemaVersion":2,"sectionID":20020432,"chapterID":15001303,"chapterNumber":"XIII-3","sectionNumber":"133-231","title":"Modification of height and setback controls","officialText":"","previewText":"Buildings or other structures may exceed the underlying height and setback regulations for a percentage of the length of each street line of the Loop Road, as follows:\n\n(a) North Loop Road - 65 percent\n\n(b) East Loop Road - 35 percent\n\n(c) West Loop Road - 35 percent\n\n(d) South Loop Road - 65 percent.\n\nFurthermore, the street line length percentages set forth in paragraphs (a) through (d) of this Section may be excee","blocks":[{"id":"zr-20432-block-001","kind":"html","html":"<p><span><strong><em>Buildings or other structures</em></strong> may exceed the underlying height and setback regulations for a percentage of the length of each <strong><em>street line</em></strong> of the <strong><em>Loop Road</em></strong>, as follows: </span></p>","plainText":"Buildings or other structures may exceed the underlying height and setback regulations for a percentage of the length of each street line of the Loop Road, as follows:"},{"id":"zr-20432-block-002","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\" class=\"pseudo-li\"><span>(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>North Loop Road</em></strong> - 65 percent</span></p>","plainText":"(a) North Loop Road - 65 percent"},{"id":"zr-20432-block-003","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span></span></p>","plainText":""},{"id":"zr-20432-block-004","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\" class=\"pseudo-li\"><span>(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>East Loop Road</em></strong> - 35 percent</span></p>","plainText":"(b) East Loop Road - 35 percent"},{"id":"zr-20432-block-005","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span></span></p>","plainText":""},{"id":"